# Store text with LF in the repository and check it out with LF on every
# platform, so that dotnet format produces the same result on Windows and
# Linux (03 A5: a formatting difference between hosts is a bug, not a quirk).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.vhdx binary
*.qcow2 binary
*.img binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF; powershell.exe 5.1 tolerates LF, but editors
# on Windows and signed script tooling expect CRLF.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
